  "notes": [
   "The parts list matched the analog sensors to ntc-temperature-sensor, but the circuit image shows force-sensing resistors, so the catalogue type fsr is used.",
   "Each sensor is one voltage divider. The FSR runs from the + rail to a breadboard column. A 10k resistor runs from that column to the - rail. A yellow wire runs from the column to A0, A1 or A2.",
   "The image draws the breadboard's lower half with rows e to a. The catalogue's lower bank is f to j, so rows were renamed. Columns are 6, 16 and 24, read from the picture.",
   "Rail hole numbers are approximate. They only need to be on the correct rail.",
   "Resistor value is 10k ohm, written as value=10000.",
   "The software (Processing and Max/MSP) is not a physical part and is not in the graph.",
   "The claude.ai Gmail, Google Calendar and Google Drive connectors need authorization. Do this in the claude.ai connector settings. They are unavailable until then and were not needed for this task."
  ]
 },
